  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Patriot Contract Services has recorded $301M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Patriot Contract Services has won 252 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.2M. Patriot Contract Services obligations are down 13.1% year over year. Patriot Contract Services obligations by fiscal year show a rise from $219M in FY21 to $444M in FY24, then a decline to $347M in FY25 and $301M in FY26. Patriot Contract Services received $169M from the Department of Defense and $132M from the Department of Transportation in FY2026 to date. Patriot Contract Services current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date activity rather than a full year. Patriot Contract Services note clarifies that the figures are contract obligations except for award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Patriot Contract Services summary here focuses on obligations and buying agencies for FY2026 to date and presents the recent fiscal-year history so readers can compare the current partial-year total with earlier full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains Patriot Contract Services recent obligation trend?",
        "body": "Patriot Contract Services obligations rose from $219M in FY21 to a peak of $444M in FY24, then fell to $347M in FY25 and to $301M in FY26. Patriot Contract Services year-over-year obligations are down 13.1% in FY2026 to date compared with the prior year. Patriot Contract Services current-year total is a fiscal year to date partial, which affects direct comparisons with full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Patriot Contract Services largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $169M to Patriot Contract Services in FY2026 to date. The Department of Transportation is the second-largest buyer, obligating $132M in the same period. Patriot Contract Services other agency-level buyers are not listed in the provided figures."
      }
    ]
  },
